WEBVTT

00:00:00.475 --> 00:00:03.553
Journey nineteen: save listings for later.

00:00:03.553 --> 00:00:08.538
A member keeps businesses, products and spaces on a private list, to

00:00:08.538 --> 00:00:13.375
find them again. This run takes the journey from ninety percent to

00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:14.035
complete.

00:00:14.892 --> 00:00:19.444
Until now, only a business page and a product page had a heart.

00:00:19.444 --> 00:00:24.647
Now every card on Browse has one too: the featured businesses, the rooms

00:00:24.647 --> 00:00:28.404
and places to stay, and the products from the shops.

00:00:29.109 --> 00:00:32.441
Joanna presses the heart on Legacy Financial.

00:00:32.441 --> 00:00:37.476
It shows pressed at once, and the toast says it is saved, with Undo.

00:00:37.476 --> 00:00:42.807
She stays on Browse: the heart sits beside the card's link, never inside

00:00:42.807 --> 00:00:43.029
it.

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:48.533
Undo, within its eight seconds, takes it off the list again, and the

00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:53.333
heart is released. Each heart names its item, so a screen reader can

00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.462
tell them apart.

00:00:55.166 --> 00:00:59.802
A space is saved as the listing it is, and a product as the product of

00:00:59.802 --> 00:01:00.398
its shop.

00:01:01.099 --> 00:01:04.441
While a save is on its way, the heart is busy.

00:01:04.441 --> 00:01:09.237
It fades, says so to assistive technology, and a second press does

00:01:09.237 --> 00:01:11.635
nothing until the server answers.

00:01:12.492 --> 00:01:17.403
The same heart is on the cards of a category, of search, and of a shop.

00:01:17.403 --> 00:01:22.037
A business already saved shows its heart pressed, filled, and named

00:01:22.037 --> 00:01:24.804
Saved, so colour is never the only sign.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.577
When Joanna signs out, her list leaves the device.

00:01:29.577 --> 00:01:34.616
Back on Browse without reloading, no heart shows what she saved.

00:01:35.319 --> 00:01:40.192
A visitor who presses a heart is asked to join or sign in, in a prompt

00:01:40.192 --> 00:01:43.743
that names the item: Join to save Luzandre dot com.

00:01:44.445 --> 00:01:49.356
She signs in, comes straight back to Browse, and the item she pressed is

00:01:49.356 --> 00:01:54.063
saved, once, without a second press. Her own list was read again from

00:01:54.063 --> 00:01:54.813
the server.

00:01:55.806 --> 00:02:00.503
Everything saved is on the page Saved, newest first, with the space

00:02:00.503 --> 00:02:05.550
among the businesses. The list is private: no other member can reach it.

00:02:06.588 --> 00:02:12.034
Behind the screen, the tests prove each criterion: hearts on every kind

00:02:12.034 --> 00:02:17.172
of card, the busy heart, the return after sign-in, and signing out.

00:02:17.172 --> 00:02:21.084
An API test proves a space is saved by its address.

00:02:21.942 --> 00:02:26.946
Journey nineteen is complete. Nothing changes in the database.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:32.031
What is left for the owner is to run the visual, responsive and

00:02:32.031 --> 00:02:33.726
accessibility sweeps.
